WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.850
Anne enjoyed her Summer wholeheartedly.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.760
She and Diana fairly lived outdoors.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:49.950
They walked, rowed, berried, and
dreamed to their heart's content.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:58.390
Marilla obeyed the doctor and offered
no objections to Anne's gypsyings.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.460
One evening,

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:11.950
Mr. Barry took Diana and Anne
to White Sand's Hotel.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.580
They went there to have dinner.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.990
The hotel was filled with many
tourists from America

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:34.600
and the hall was brightly decorated with
the newly invented electric lights.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:03.100
Then one day, just as the Summer holidays
were coming to an end...

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.920
Idlewild was a beautiful ring of white
birch trees where Anne and Diana

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:34.960
had played for the first time after
they became good friends.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.460
They were shocked after seeing

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.250
how the place where they haven't
been for so long had changed.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.190
Is this Idlewild?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.320
I can't belive this.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:52.140
Our wonderful memories have
become such a sorry sight.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:52.450
Nostalgic memories of that
time came to their minds

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:58.050
and both of them sat down and wept.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:05.150
The tears carried sweetness and sadness
of their childhood memories.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:25.150
On the last day of her Summer holidays,
Anne went to the attic

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:28.250
to get her school books from the old trunk

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.870
and she missed them so much that
she talked to them.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:44.160
You good old friends, I'm glad to
see your honest faces once more.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.390
Yes, even you, geometry.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:57.070
Marilla, I've had a perfectly beautiful summer.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.830
You've regain your health, Anne.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.930
I feel just like studying with might and main.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.730
Look, I've already got them back.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.560
Wish me luck!

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.890
I'm going!

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.360
Anne, hurry, hurry!

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:42.530
Good morning, Diana, Minnie May!

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.430
Minnie May, that really suits you.

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.060
You're now a Year One student.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:51.900
Work hard.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:52.500
Yes.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.190
Look, it's my lunch.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:57.460
I'm already hungry. I'll eat it right now.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:02.200
Oh! Minnie May, you're supposed
to eat it with the others in school.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.140
Understood?

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.570
Then, let's go Minnie May.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.280
Yes.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.440
Alright, Minnie May, put yours too.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:52.320
Yes.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:09.260
Miss Stacy was glad to find all her
pupils eager for work once more.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:15.290
Especially did the Queen's class
gird up their loins for the fray.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:21.750
And the rivalry between Anne and Gilbert
has become more intense than ever.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.440
Anne Shirley, come to the blackboard
and answer the next question, please.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:25.990
Yes.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:50.350
Do you know what time it is?

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:53.370
You mustn't overwork yourself.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.290
Marilla, I keep thinking about Gil...

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:00.440
...about the others who are still studying
at this hour and I can't sleep.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:01.700
My, my.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:07.150
Don't oversleep and go out without having
time to wash the dishes again tomorrow.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:09.960
I know, Marilla.
I'll go to sleep soon.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.060
Well, goodnight.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.060
Goodnight.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.200
Anne!

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:18.860
Anne!

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:22.640
What's the matter, Marilla?

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:26.560
Anne, come down and help me pick apples.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.180
Yes, all right.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.740
It's good to have a change sometimes.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.570
You're right, Marilla, I feel great now.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.940
It's good that you take
your studies seriously

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.320
but you have to watch your health too.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:12:01.000
If you get sick, you won't be able to attend
school and all your work will be for naught.

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:02.650
Don't worry, Marilla.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.980
I've stored lots of energy
during the summer holidays.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:08.190
I couldn't be healthier.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:15.740
Marilla was always
worried about Anne's health.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:21.810
But never mentioned to her about her own
head aches and Matthew's heart problems.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:41.360
Matthew, smoking is bad for the health.
Don't you know that?

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.160
Don't worry about that.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:49.590
And the doctor also advised you
not to work so hard.

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:51.730
Don't work too hard.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:53.270
All right.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:58.870
Maybe we should hire another
boy to help pick the potatoes.

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.410
Well now...

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.160
I'll think about it.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:09.000
My heart it's not the only problem, Marilla.
You should take your headaches seriously.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:17.810
I'll go for a check-up one of this days.
We're getting old. We have to be careful.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.040
That's true.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.810
Thank goodness!
We did it!

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.160
I did it!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.460
No. It's not there.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.910
My name's not on it.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:48.280
It was just a dream.
Thank goodness!

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:55.150
Anne dreamed about the school results.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:16:00.830
Gilbert's name was printed in first place

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:05.010
and Anne couldn't find her name anywhere.

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:11.330
It was just a dream but for Anne
was a horrifying nightmare.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.090
Good morning, Anne.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:30.560
Good morning.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.770
Is there something wrong, Anne?
You look pale.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.020
It's nothing.

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:44.230
Anne, I'm going to Carmody
today to buy some things.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:45.200
Is that so?

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:49.610
Today it's my turn to
hold the Story Club meeting.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:53.320
Alright. You can treat your guests
with the cake you baked yesterday.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:54.560
All right.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:59.100
The Story Club was
formed a year and a half ago.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:03.880
They came up with the idea when
they had to write a story for school.

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:12.410
Diana, Ruby and Jane,
lost all interest in writing stories,

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.340
but they liked the excuse
to get everyone together,

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.500
and so the Story Club persisted.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:24.350
Especially, Diana. For
since the Queens Class was formed,

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:28.990
she hardly got to
chat with the three friends.

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:35.120
So she always looked forward to
the tea gathering held once a month.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.270
Diana is so late.

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.490
Yes, she is.

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:41.150
Say, what if we cancel today's session?

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:43.470
I want to prepare for history class.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:48.910
Oh, but didn't you want to discuss with
Diana about the brooch for your new clothes?

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:52.270
That's right. It's not nice
if we don't wait for Diana to come.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:54.530
But History is my worst subject.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:58.410
I'm not in the mood to
waste time here chatting.

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:03.200
Ruby, are you saying that
we should quit the Story Club?

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.200
Y-yes.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:08.830
I don't feel like writing stories.
No one here has written one recently too.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:12.620
All we do is sit and chat.
It's quite meaningless.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.820
Jane, what about you?

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.300
Do you also think we should quit?

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.070
Well, I don't really care about the Story Club.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:27.660
But it would be a pity if we don't even get a
chance to have tea and talk about girls' stuff.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:29.420
Of course I feel the same way.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:35.860
But lately I've been feeling uneasy
whenever I help doing housework.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:40.810
I keep thinking of my studies and
feel that I don't have time for such matters.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:47.440
And when I sit in class, I'm tired and I want
to get out to go to bed as soon as possible.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:51.780
Ruby, that's exactly what I feel.

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:55.150
Sometimes I worry that I
won't be able to pass the exam

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:58.170
and I get so nervous that
I can't even sleep at night.

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.660
Anne wouldn't understand how we feel.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.810
Oh, that's not true.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:06.800
This morning I had a nightmare
in which I had failed.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:10.510
And all of you got in.
Only my name wasn't on it.

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:11.760
Impossible!

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:12.660
It's true.

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:16.820
If you couldn't get in,
we would be even worse.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.260
Don't you think so, Jane?

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.520
Of course.

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:23.690
But if Anne worries about it too,
I feel a little better.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:24.690
Of course I do.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:28.190
Can we stop talking about exams?

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:31.690
It's making me uncomfortable.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.280
It's all because Diana didn't turn up.

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:38.160
Because if she was here,
we wouldn't be talking about this.

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:39.640
That's true.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.570
It's a pity that
she decided not to go to Queens.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:47.320
Oh, but I tell everything to Diana about
the exams as well as other matters.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.830
That's because Diana and you are best friends.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:52.340
Diana is really late.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.390
I'm going home.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.330
We don't have so much free time like her.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:19:59.490
That's true.

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.220
Then I'll go home too.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.320
Wait!

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:07.100
I have nothing to say if you want
to quit the Story Club

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:10.550
but it's not fair to decide on it without Diana.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.200
That's quite true.

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:16.110
I'll get Diana.
Wait just a little.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:25.090
Oh, Diana, you're here?

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:28.740
We were waiting for you, Diana.
Where were you?

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.500
You'll be fined for being late.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.710
What's wrong, Diana?
Has something happened at home?

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:40.160
Stop pretending.

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:43.000
I heard everything you said.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.170
I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:49.240
I just wanted to play a trick on you.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:52.950
But I couldn't help
getting upset as I listened.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.110
And then...

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.260
And then...

00:20:58.220 --> 00:20:59.210
Diana...

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:02.460
I'm different from all of you.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:07.120
While all of you are busy over exams,
I'm the only one getting lonely.

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:13.900
I really like this club.
I didn't want to be late.

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:19.980
But... but... my singing teacher came to visit.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:25.830
I didn't want to keep you waiting
so I sent her off hurriedly.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:29.520
But now this club will end.

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:31.160
That's not true, Diana.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.370
Enough!

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:35.650
I don't want to interrupt your studies.

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:39.340
I now realize that those days

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:46.550
we used to write about love, murder,
dreams and other matters are over.

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:47.920
Isn't that right, Anne?

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.890
It's no use to carry on with
the club for formality's sake.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.600
Ruby is right.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.790
It's meaningless.

00:21:58.130 --> 00:21:58.960
Diana.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:05.700
I'm sorry, Diana!

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:53.870
Marilla, when did you come back?

00:22:54.180 --> 00:22:58.430
I called you but you didn't reply.
I thought you were walking Diana home.

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:00.060
And the tea?

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:01.620
I've got it ready.

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:03.220
I'm sorry.

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:14.910
Please, go tell Matthew that the tea is ready.

00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:16.350
Marilla...

00:23:17.380 --> 00:23:18.410
Are you surprised?

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:19.620
Yes...

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:21.840
It looks strange?

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.150
No.

00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:25.700
It feels a bit uncomfortable in this part.

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:28.480
You'll get used to it.

00:23:29.960 --> 00:23:33.500
Today I went to Doctor Spencer in Carmody.

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:37.970
He said I may be getting
headaches because of my eyesight.

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.220
It'll be a blessing if the migrane
can be cured just like that.

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:45.090
I'll go get Matthew.

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:11.210
Anne feels that she
has matured somehow today.

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:19.750
Spring visits Green Gables again.

00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:24.280
Marilla senses Anne's growth
and can't help feeling lonely.

00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:27.350
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.430 --> 00:24:28.920
A 15 Years Old Spring

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:29.950
Please watch!
